{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"And you shall take of the first of all the fruit of the ground which you shall bring from your land\"</b> — that you shall take of the first of all the fruit that you bring into the house, from your land which HaShem your Elohim gives you — is that He commands that he designate the fruit in the field and pronounce a name over it, and bring it to his house and place it in a suitable vessel for carrying it to the Chosen House. And Scripture gives no measure for them, but even a single grain of any given species exempts the entire field, like the law of תרומה (heave-offering), where one wheat-grain exempts the entire pile." "<b>\"And you shall go to the place which HaShem your Elohim shall choose\"</b> — according to its plain sense, it warns that you may not offer first fruits in any of your gates before the House is chosen, for just as He warned regarding slaughter outside [the Temple precincts] in the case of sacrifices, so too He warns regarding first fruits. But the obligation of first fruits applies immediately after they conquered and divided [the land], according to the words of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 26:1). And in the Sifrei (Tavo 2): \"And you shall go to the place which HaShem your Elohim shall choose to cause His name to dwell there\" — this is Shiloh and the Eternal House. Now perhaps one might say that the high places were forbidden during both these periods, but they would also offer first fruits in Nov and Gibeon; however, they are not offered at a private bamah, for it is written \"altar.\" And perhaps from what is written (Exodus 23:19), \"The first of the first fruits of your land you shall bring to the house of HaShem your Elohim\" — they were not offered in the Tent or the Tabernacle but only at Shiloh, where there was a house of stone, and in the Eternal House."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :register {:flags {1 ["the Eternal"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:55:49.177523568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}